IMPORT prelude

-- Limitation Act 2005 (WA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The Act counts periods in whole years ("if 6 years have elapsed since the cause of
-- action accrued", s 13) and by age ("if the person has reached 21 years of age", s 31); the extension and suspension
-- provisions add plain days (ss 32, 35).
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "Limitation Act 2005", State of Western
-- Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Limitation Act 2005`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `is after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day before` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` MINUS 1)

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is after` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is before` `the second day`
    THEN `the first day`
    ELSE `the second day`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The same day and month a number of years later; 29 February falls on 28 February in a year that has none (fork F1 in
-- NOTES.md). With the day of the event excluded (the Interpretation Act 1984 rule, not deposited), n years from day D end at the
-- end of this day, so it is the last day on which the action can be commenced.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the anniversary` n `years after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the days in month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `of` `the target year`)) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS n

-- The day a person born on a day reaches an age: the birthday (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER, `the birth day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day of reaching age` `the age` `for birth on` `the birth day` MEANS `the anniversary` `the age` `years after` `the birth day`
